A||||8||STUK'N'80s||180 degree thermostat||||5||
Z||000000||STUK'N'80s||09-02-2001||03:39 PM||||Does anyone know where I can obtain a HYPERTECH 180 degree thermostat to complement my Low temp. Hypertech fan switch that I recently installed into my 85 GT.  I tried Summitracing but they don't have that part anymore.  Is there another reputable high performance brand that I should consider if Hypertech brand thermostat proves to be elusive??||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||09-02-2001||05:18 PM||||Check Rodney Dickman's site.  <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/retail.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com/retail.html</A> <BR>He carries Stant thermostats in 180*. <BR>Good guy to deal with.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000002||Formula88||09-02-2001||06:47 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com</A> <BR>I have nothing but great things to say about Rodney.  I also have his 180* thermostat and 195* fan switch in my car and couldn't be happier.<P>The Hypertech fan switches are 176*, so you'd need to go with a 160* thermostat.  I believe Rodney has them, but if not, I know the Fiero Store does.  <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierostore.com</A> <P>Personally, I think a 160* thermo is a bit cold for a stock engine, so I'd recommend getting Rodney's 180* thermo and 195* fan switch.  It's a great combo!<p>[This message has been edited by Formula88 (edited 09-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||09-02-2001||09:44 PM||||You can get them at any auto parts store as long as the guys working there know how to do their job. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||3fifty||09-03-2001||10:52 PM||||I agree with Formula88. I took my 160 thermo out and put the 180 in. I was getting check engine with the 160 in a 85 2.8 GT with the low temp fan switch.<P>3fifty one day!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Philphine||09-04-2001||12:50 AM||||i just got a stant 180deg. today at pepboys. when i looked it up in the stant book it didn't list it but when i went to the display to get one it was there beside the 195deg. ones.||||reg||1
Z||000006||StuGood||09-04-2001||10:30 AM||||Not a fancy upscale supplier or anything, but  my local AutoZonk   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> carries them.<P>And if you need something to complement a low temp. fan switch, you can always do it yourself!  As in, "Hey, you're a really cool fan switch..."   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 09-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Bruce||09-04-2001||11:09 AM||||If you find an easy way to get the old fan switch out, let me know!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Formula88||09-04-2001||11:40 AM||||Just put a socket over the fan switch and take it out.  The hard part is getting your fingers in there to release the wire connector.  I just had to fight with it till I could get it off.||||reg||1
